      "side": 1,
      "message": "id_bits is whatever the host last wrote to GICR_PROPBASER, so at 0 or 1 the division gives 0 and pend_sz is 0. hyp_share_pin_mem then has num_pages 0, shares nothing and pins an empty range, and enable_lpi goes on to write the host\u0027s GICR_PENDBASER to the hardware and enable LPIs.\n\nThat leaves the redistributor enabled against a pending table we have neither shared nor pinned, at an address the host chose and is free to donate to a guest afterwards. The id_bits clamp from the property table patch would close this too, if the lower end is bounded and not just the upper.",
